  "result": "Shell completion now handles arguments containing `#` correctly, and the 69 tests in `tests/test_parser.py` and `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass. I didn't run the full suite, and I didn't confirm that the new end-to-end test fails without the fix.\n\n- **Fix:** in `src/click/shell_completion.py`, `split_arg_string` now sets `lex.commenters = \"\"`, so `#` is no longer treated as a comment and `cli a#b c` splits into `[\"cli\", \"a#b\", \"c\"]`.\n- **Tests:**\n  - `tests/test_parser.py`: three new `split_arg_string` cases: `a#b`, a leading `#b`, and `a#b` inside an unclosed quote.\n  - `tests/test_shell_completion.py`: a new end-to-end bash completion test, `test_complete_args_with_hash`, with a `#` value followed by a partial option.\n- **Changelog:** `CHANGES.md` has a new unreleased 8.5.1 entry.",
